      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Showcase your skills on your resume and know your resume inside out. Design your resume on latex, use this template - Jake's Resume Here’s my resume for Reference - Mohit-Tech-Resume",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Maintain Good cgpa, this was one of the issues i faced a lot during placement season as i was not able to apply for around 6 companies due to low cgpa. Later when cgpa was updated after 6th sem, i was able to sit for all further companies. 8+ cgpa is completely safe but 7.5 will also allow you to sit for 90% of the companies.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Practice DSA way before placement starts and when placements come close, you can focus on your revision more rather than learning new skills.",
          "category": "Coding preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Be strong at CS-Core fundamentals and build projects which make some impact, it will surely impress interviewers.",
          "category": "Project preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Don't forget to attend PPTs of companies which you apply, it helps a lott to know about the company and also if you interact with presenters, they will surely remember your face during the interview.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Practice Guestimates ,Puzzles and Aptitude Questions beforehand.",
          "category": "OA preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Prepare common HR questions in advance. I had created a sheet of possible questions with my own answers, which helped me a lot. I also requested my already-placed friends to conduct mock interviews—this gave me valuable feedback and helped me self-reflect and improve.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Have Patience During Placements, If you have worked hard on your skills, you will surely get selected. Placements also involve a great deal of luck.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 3
        }
      ],
