      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "For project-related discussions, it’s really helpful to use the STAR method—first explain the situation your project was solving, then your role or task, the actions you took (technologies, code, concepts used), and finally the result or outcome.",
          "category": "Project preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Make sure to be thorough with your resume and the skills you have mentioned, because interviewers often dive deep into whatever is listed.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "When discussing projects, including details about the code and how it works can make your explanation more clear and convincing.",
          "category": "Project preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Be well-prepared with common HR questions, as most companies ask similar questions.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Always ask a question at the end of the interview—it shows that you are genuinely interested in learning more about the company and its culture.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Be confident while answering; do not appear hesitant or unsure.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Maintain a positive attitude and always have a smile on your face throughout the interview.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Start preparing at least one month before placements to build confidence and speed.",
          "category": "OA preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Speak clearly and confidently during interviews. Avoid filler words and maintain a steady pace.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "While solving coding or technical problems, explain your thought process aloud.",
          "category": "Coding preparation",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Pay attention to the interviewer’s questions and respond accordingly. Don’t interrupt; it shows respect and good listening skills.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Trust that everything happens for a reason. Stay calm and positive throughout the preparation and interview process.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        }
